# Example only. start.cmd makes the real one on the first run, next to this file:
#     kaggle-coder\.env      (git ignores any file named .env, so it is never uploaded)
# Never put a real key or token in this example file: it goes to GitHub.
# Your Kaggle API token is separate: it goes in %USERPROFILE%\.kaggle\access_token (setup.cmd does this).
#
# Every line below is OPTIONAL. Leave a line out and the default shown is used.
# A wrong value stops start.cmd with a message that names the line and what is allowed.

# Made for you on the first run (32 or more letters and numbers). Nothing to do.
# CODER_API_KEY=made-for-you-by-start.cmd

# --- timers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDLE_MINUTES=10        turn the AI off after this many minutes without a question (5 to 60)
# BLOCK_MINUTES=ask      "ask" = at each start, ask "how long will you code? 30, 45 or 60".
#                        A number (0 to 120) skips the question: 0 = no block, just the idle rule.
#                        During a block the AI stays up through quiet pauses; afterwards IDLE_MINUTES applies.
# MAX_HOURS=2            never run longer than this, whatever else is set (0.5 to 6)
# START_WAIT_MINUTES=20  give up (and clean up) if Kaggle has not started you after this long (5 to 60)

# --- the AI (advanced: change only if Corey says so) --------------------------------------
# MODEL=A                A = the big model. A-small = a smaller one, if A runs out of GPU memory.
# CONTEXT_TOKENS=65536   Cline's "Context Window Size" must show the same number (8192 to 131072)
# MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=8192 Cline's "Max Output Tokens" must show the same number (1024 to 32768)
# SELF_TEST=0            1 = after READY, check tool calls and the prompt cache (uses a minute of GPU)

# --- permanent address (optional; double-click fixed-address\fixed-address.cmd to fill these in)
# FIXED_HOST=kaggle.gamelab.link
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
# CF_KV_NAMESPACE_ID=your-kv-namespace-id
# CF_KV_TOKEN=a-token-that-can-only-edit-that-one-store
